FINAL ANSWER:
Not quite one person, but close to it. Andrew Gallant owns about two-thirds of the surviving Rust lines, and Sam Okoro has most of the rest.

I ran `git blame -w -M -C` on HEAD across the 10 tracked `.rs` files, which hold 4,366 lines in total.

| Rank | Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Andrew Gallant | 2,838 | 65.0% |
| 2 | Sam Okoro | 646 | 14.8% |
| 3 | Inès Moreau and Ines Moreau (probably one person) | 217 (120 + 97) | 5.0% |
| 4 | Sebastian Thiel | 74 | 1.7% |
| 5 | Ashley | 68 | 1.6% |
| 6 | Aron Griffis | 59 | 1.4% |

Further down are mcharsley (45), Marvin Löbel (41) and Martin Sehnoutka (38).

- **Moreau:** Git lists two names with two emails, `ines@moreau.example` and `ines.moreau@university.example`. The repo has no `.mailmap`, so git does not merge them. I assumed they are the same person, but I haven't confirmed it. If they are separate people, each is about 2–3% and the third place goes to Sebastian Thiel (1.7%) or Ashley (1.6%).
- **Concentration:** The top two authors hold about 80% of the lines. Beyond them, ownership is spread thinly across many contributors.

