FINAL ANSWER:
Authorship is concentrated but not single-person. Andrew Gallant owns about 65% of the surviving Rust lines.

Counts come from `git blame` over the 10 tracked `.rs` files, 4,366 lines in total. I ignored the line-ending normalization commit (`c862f48`) and the SPDX header commit (`a45246e`), and I ignored whitespace changes. Without that, those two commits would have been credited with most lines.

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Andrew Gallant | 2,843 | 65.1% |
| Sam Okoro | 647 | 14.8% |
| Inès Moreau | 218 | 5.0% |
| Sebastian Thiel | 74 | 1.7% |
| Ashley | 68 | 1.6% |
| Aron Griffis | 59 | 1.4% |

- **Merged aliases:** Inès Moreau is the sum of "Inès Moreau" (121) and "Ines Moreau" (97). I assumed those are the same person, based only on the matching name. Treating them as separate would put them at 2.8% and 2.2%.
- **Long tail:** Another 30 or so contributors hold the remaining 13%, mostly with fewer than 50 lines each.
- **Bus factor:** Gallant and Okoro together hold about 80%. If either left, the remaining knowledge of most of the Rust code would sit with a few people.

